{"call_id":"call_AIEIVFZ2ewgAkYlryZZ210V7","process_id":"48367","turn_id":"019ca84b-f46d-7723-9d53-aa223b2f1142","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task start @01KJDQ1GZ --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task start @01KJDQ1GZ --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Started task: 01KJDQ1GZ\",\"task\":{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\"slugs\":[],\"title\":\"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\"type\":\"task\",\"description\":\"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\"spec_ref\":\"@daemon-server\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"context\":[],\"priority\":3,\"tags\":[],\"vcs_refs\":[],\"session_id\":\"01KJKWXHKKHZMP574E78F7BHA3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\"started_at\":\"2026-03-01T07:29:06.129Z\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:53:35.116Z\",\"notes\":[{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\"author\":\"@claude\",\"content\":\"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\"author\":\"@claude\",\"content\":\"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2DPN621APMNNFFZCX3RN5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:47:24.582Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Execution context:\\n- Background: Web UI websocket manager can enter reconnect churn due to stale onclose handlers from prior sockets and reconnect attempts after intentional disconnect.\\n- Scope: stabilize client connection lifecycle for intentional close and project-switch reconnects; add focused regression tests for stale-close and manual-disconnect behavior.\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts, tests/web-ui/websocket-manager.test.ts (new).\\n- Verification: run targeted vitest for websocket manager tests and relevant existing connection-related tests, then run full npm test before submit.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2R4EQV8T6WJV405GP3XWQ\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:53:06.391Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Implemented WebSocket reconnect-stability fix in packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts and added regression tests in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- Added stale-socket guards in connect() event handlers so late events from old sockets are ignored and cannot null out the active connection.\\n- Added intentionalDisconnect tracking so manual disconnects do not schedule reconnect attempts.\\n- Updated disconnect() to detach current socket reference before close, preventing close-handler races with new connections.\\n- Added regression tests for:\\n  1) old-socket close after project switch does not disrupt active socket,\\n  2) intentional disconnect does not auto-reconnect,\\n  3) unexpected disconnect still triggers reconnect.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed)\\n- npm test (fails on pre-existing baseline issues unrelated to this change):\\n  - tests/cli-serve.test.ts \\\"should show No projects registered when no projects exist\\\"\\n  - tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout failures (2 cases)\\n- kspec validate (pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues)\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2TCM0Y1NCBBZ9JZTKW183\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:54:20.288Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Submitted for review in PR #622: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/622 (branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race, commit 155276ca9). Implemented WebSocketManager stale-close race guard and intentional-disconnect reconnect suppression with regression coverage in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed). Full npm test and kspec validate still show pre-existing unrelated baseline failures/issues (cli-serve no-projects assertion, session-note-limit timeouts, existing validate schema/reference/alignment/completeness warnings/errors).\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM385VE2C92BYG0GM4HK06T\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T07:01:52.110Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 failed regression gate. npm test reports 3 failures (tests/cli-serve.test.ts foreground startup assertion; tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts two timeout failures). Review posted with inline comment; do not merge until full suite is green.\",\"supersedes\":null}],\"todos\":[],\"automation\":\"eligible\",\"_sourceFile\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"}}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Started task: 01KJDQ1GZ\",\"task\":{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\"slugs\":[],\"title\":\"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\"type\":\"task\",\"description\":\"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\"spec_ref\":\"@daemon-server\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"context\":[],\"priority\":3,\"tags\":[],\"vcs_refs\":[],\"session_id\":\"01KJKWXHKKHZMP574E78F7BHA3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\"started_at\":\"2026-03-01T07:29:06.129Z\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:53:35.116Z\",\"notes\":[{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\"author\":\"@claude\",\"content\":\"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\"author\":\"@claude\",\"content\":\"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2DPN621APMNNFFZCX3RN5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:47:24.582Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Execution context:\\n- Background: Web UI websocket manager can enter reconnect churn due to stale onclose handlers from prior sockets and reconnect attempts after intentional disconnect.\\n- Scope: stabilize client connection lifecycle for intentional close and project-switch reconnects; add focused regression tests for stale-close and manual-disconnect behavior.\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts, tests/web-ui/websocket-manager.test.ts (new).\\n- Verification: run targeted vitest for websocket manager tests and relevant existing connection-related tests, then run full npm test before submit.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2R4EQV8T6WJV405GP3XWQ\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:53:06.391Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Implemented WebSocket reconnect-stability fix in packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts and added regression tests in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- Added stale-socket guards in connect() event handlers so late events from old sockets are ignored and cannot null out the active connection.\\n- Added intentionalDisconnect tracking so manual disconnects do not schedule reconnect attempts.\\n- Updated disconnect() to detach current socket reference before close, preventing close-handler races with new connections.\\n- Added regression tests for:\\n  1) old-socket close after project switch does not disrupt active socket,\\n  2) intentional disconnect does not auto-reconnect,\\n  3) unexpected disconnect still triggers reconnect.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed)\\n- npm test (fails on pre-existing baseline issues unrelated to this change):\\n  - tests/cli-serve.test.ts \\\"should show No projects registered when no projects exist\\\"\\n  - tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout failures (2 cases)\\n- kspec validate (pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues)\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM2TCM0Y1NCBBZ9JZTKW183\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T06:54:20.288Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Submitted for review in PR #622: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/622 (branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race, commit 155276ca9). Implemented WebSocketManager stale-close race guard and intentional-disconnect reconnect suppression with regression coverage in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed). Full npm test and kspec validate still show pre-existing unrelated baseline failures/issues (cli-serve no-projects assertion, session-note-limit timeouts, existing validate schema/reference/alignment/completeness warnings/errors).\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJM385VE2C92BYG0GM4HK06T\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T07:01:52.110Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 failed regression gate. npm test reports 3 failures (tests/cli-serve.test.ts foreground startup assertion; tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts two timeout failures). Review posted with inline comment; do not merge until full suite is green.\",\"supersedes\":null}],\"todos\":[],\"automation\":\"eligible\",\"_sourceFile\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":153525493},"formatted_output":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Started task: 01KJDQ1GZ\",\"task\":{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\"slugs\":[],\"title\":\"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\"type\":\"task\